-- title:
--   Geometric fibres of the two-chart model of X₁(Mp) are connected
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M \ge 5$ with $\mathrm{NeZero}\,M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{p\}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma1 (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) of $X_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as fraction field, with $p$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ in the image of $A \to L$, and with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible via $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero (as a `Fact`) with image in $L((q))$ equal to [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot(\text{power series})$ of the $j$-invariant. The assertion: for every algebraically closed field $k$ and every morphism $x : \operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, the underlying topological space of the pullback of [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) along $x$ is a connected space (in particular nonempty). Here [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) is the morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ obtained from the pushout [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229) of `fFin` and `fInf` by descending the two maps $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure morphisms $A \to \mathrm{chartAlg}\,A\,K\,\{j\}$ and $A \to \mathrm{chartAlg}\,A\,K\,\{j^{-1}\}$.
--
--   This is the connectedness of all geometric fibres of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over the localisation of $\mathbb{Z}[\zeta_p]$ at a prime above $p$: the generic fibre is geometrically connected because $L$ is algebraically closed in the $q$-expansion function field, and the fibre at the closed point is connected because the reduction consists of components meeting each other. It feeds the later analysis of sections, relative Picard classes and level polynomials for this model, where connected geometric fibres are needed to control the relative Jacobian.
